### Storage RBAC role assignments (D25 — the "cleaner half" of the split-auth posture)

These role assignments give the Container App's system-assigned MI Entra-RBAC access to the storage account from Sprint 1.3. **No storage account key or connection string is involved on the transcoder side — ever (D25).**

| Role | Assignee | Scope | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Storage Blob Data Contributor` | Container App MI Principal ID (above) | `stmusicslaylistdevuse2` storage account | Read raw-uploads, write finished (Epic 6) |
| `Storage Table Data Contributor` | Container App MI Principal ID (above) | `stmusicslaylistdevuse2` storage account | Update `Songs` records (flip `processing` → `ready` or `failed`) |

**Scope is the storage account, NOT the subscription, NOT the resource group** — least-privilege per the project's D25/D30 RBAC discipline.

**Used by:** Sprint 6.0 (build/push pipeline updates the Container App revision). Sprint 6.1 (transcode logic uses `DefaultAzureCredential` / equivalent SDK pattern that finds the system-assigned MI automatically). Sprint 6.3 (real ffmpeg image deploys; first end-to-end test). Sprint 7.x (KEDA queue-triggered scaling on this app; queue from Sprint 1.5).

## Storage Queues (inside the storage account from Sprint 1.3)

Lives inside `stmusicslaylistdevuse2`. No global uniqueness, no prefix per `infra/naming-convention.md`.

| Queue | Purpose | Populated by | Drained by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `transcode-jobs` | Main work queue. Event Grid drops blob-created messages here when a raw upload lands in `raw-uploads`. | Sprint 7.1's event subscription (Event Grid → queue, via the Event Grid topic MI) | Sprint 7.2's Container App + Sprint 6.1's transcoder logic |
| `transcode-jobs-poison` | **Dead-letter queue per D6.** Storage Queue has no native DLQ; the transcoder's app logic (Sprint 7.2) tracks dequeue-count per message and moves "poison" messages here after a configured maximum is exceeded, then flips the song record's state to `failed`. | Sprint 7.2's app logic (move-from-main-queue when max-dequeue exceeded) | Operator inspection / forensics. Optional drain via re-enqueue if the root cause is fixed. |

**Why pre-create the poison queue at 1.5 (not 7.2):** matches the established "all stores exist before they're needed" pattern (D33's `table-backups` container at 1.3, populated by Sprint 4.4). Sprint 7.2 implements the move-to-poison logic against a known destination; no naming decision deferred into that sprint.

**Queue properties (defaults):** message TTL 7 days, max message size 64 KB. Both defaults are fine — Sprint 7.2's dead-letter logic moves messages out before TTL anyway; transcode job messages are small JSON (`songId` + blob path).

**Diagnostic settings:** Storage queue operations are captured by the storage account's `diag-queue-to-law-dev` diagnostic setting (Sprint 1.5 Step 6), forwarding StorageRead + StorageWrite + StorageDelete + Transaction metrics to `log-music-slaylist-dev-use2` (D24's third storage feeder leg, joining blob + table from Sprint 1.3).

